{"term":"canvas","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:c6c7584b69669c93bb","definition":"A type of coarse cloth, woven from hemp (traditionally) or from cotton and polyesters, useful for making sails, tents, and overcoats or as a surface for paintings.","example":"The term canvas is very widely used, as well to denote the coarse fabrics employed for kitchen use, as for strainers, and wraps for meat, as for the best quality of ordinary table and shirting linen.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["blank canvas","canvasback","canvasboard","canvasful","canvasless","canvaslike","canvasman","canvassy","Canvastown","canvaswork","empty canvas","Java canvas","new canvas","noncanvas","on the canvas","under canvas","value proposition canvas"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canvas#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6c11886c14bbf6fa79","definition":"A piece of such cloth stretched across a frame on which one may paint an artwork.","example":"She is painting a moonlight scene on the canvas.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["blank canvas","canvasback","canvasboard","canvasful","canvasless","canvaslike","canvasman","canvassy","Canvastown","canvaswork","empty canvas","Java canvas","new canvas","noncanvas","on the canvas","under canvas","value proposition canvas"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canvas#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a388c2987ac77b158f","definition":"A mesh of loosely woven cotton strands or molded plastic to be decorated with needlepoint, cross-stitch, rug hooking, or other crafts.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["blank canvas","canvasb